01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
Nightwatching is a 2007 film about the artist Rembrandt and the
creation of his 1642 painting The Night Watch.

11
01:10:42,857 --> 01:10:48,857
The film is directed by Peter Greenaway and stars Martin Freeman as Rembrandt, with Eva Birthistle as his wife Saskia van
Uylenburg, Jodhi May as his lover Geertje Dircx, and Emily Holmes as his other lover Hendrickje Stoffels.

12
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
Reinier van Brummelen is the director of photography.

13
01:23:34,285 --> 01:23:40,285
James Willcock, known for his esoteric sets,  is the art director.

14
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The film is described by co-producer Jean Labadie as "a return to the Greenaway of The Draughtsman's
Contract." It features Greenaway's trademark neoclassical compositions and graphic sexuality.

15
01:36:25,714 --> 01:36:31,714
The music is by Włodek Pawlik.

16
01:42:51,428 --> 01:42:57,428
The film premiered in competition, at the Venice Film Festival.

17
01:49:17,142 --> 01:49:23,142
Nightwatching is the first feature in Greenaway's film series "Dutch
Masters", and was followed by Goltzius and the Pelican Company.

18
01:55:42,857 --> 01:55:48,857
An associated work by the same director is the documentary film Rembrandt's J'Accuse (2008), in which Greenaway
addresses 34 "mysteries" associated with the painting, illustrated by scenes from the drama.

19
02:02:08,571 --> 02:02:14,571
The film explores themes of painter, biography, rembrandt, drama.

20
02:08:34,285 --> 02:08:40,285
The tone is emotional.
